  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Decided to encode Ethiopian 12-hour counting (hours start at 6 a.m./6 p.m.), since that is the everyday convention for Oromo speakers in Ethiopia: hours rotated so 13:00 -> 'sa'aatii torba', 9:00 -> 'sa'aatii sadii', 12:30 -> 'sa'aatii jaha fi walakkaa'. Patterns 'sa'aatii {h}' + 'fi daqiiqaa <n>' (shan, kudhan, kudha shan, digdama, digdamii shan, soddomii shan, afurtama, afurtamii shan, shantama, shantamii shan), :30 = 'fi walakkaa'. Used 'daqiiqaa kudha shan' for :15 rather than the loan 'ruubii'. Additive forms for :35-:55. Compromise: Oromo speakers outside Ethiopia (Kenya) use Western hours; the schema cannot distinguish."
    }
  ]
